# Files excluded from the distributed plugin.
#
# Everything listed here stays in the Git repository but is kept out of the ZIP
# that users download. Without it, every install would carry ~2,400 lines of test
# harness, the build specification, and a pair of 600KB banner PNGs that only
# WordPress.org ever reads.
#
# Respected by `10up/action-wordpress-plugin-deploy` and by `wp dist-archive`.
# Note that the plugin's own `assets/` directory is NOT listed: admin.css and
# admin.js are enqueued at runtime and must ship.

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.distignore

# WordPress.org listing assets — these go to SVN assets/, not into the plugin
.wordpress-org

# Development and test tooling
tests
phpcs.xml.dist
.wp-env.json
.wp-env.override.json
composer.json
composer.lock
vendor
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json

# Project documentation that is not user-facing.
# README.md and readme.txt DO ship — readme.txt is what WordPress.org parses.
SPEC.md
CONTEXT.md

# The migration is generated by `wp supabase schema --print` at runtime and shown
# on the diagnostics page, so the committed copy is a reference for the repo
# rather than something the plugin reads.
supabase

# Editors and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.log
